# Public Profile Sharing Features - Implementation Specification

## 1. Problem Statement

RawDrive already has a comprehensive public profile system with personal profiles (`/u/:slug`), company profiles (`/p/:slug`), share links, SEO support, vCard export, QR codes, and more. However, several enhancement gaps exist: profile analytics/view tracking, profile discovery directory, and custom domain support are not fully implemented.

## 2. User Story

As a **photographer using RawDrive**, I want to **track how many people view my public profile and understand visitor engagement**, so that **I can measure the effectiveness of my public presence and marketing efforts**.

## 3. Acceptance Criteria

### Happy Path - Profile Analytics
- **GIVEN** a photographer has a public profile at `/u/my-slug`
- **WHEN** a visitor views the profile page
- **THEN** the view is tracked anonymously (no PII collection)
- **AND** the photographer can see view counts in their profile settings

### Happy Path - View Statistics Dashboard
- **GIVEN** a photographer accesses their profile settings
- **WHEN** they navigate to the analytics section
- **THEN** they see total views, views by date, and basic geographic distribution
- **AND** data is displayed for the last 30 days

### Edge Case - Private Profile
- **GIVEN** a profile is set to `is_public: false`
- **WHEN** someone attempts to access the profile URL
- **THEN** no view is tracked (profile not accessible)

### Error Handling - Rate Limiting
- **GIVEN** a profile is receiving excessive traffic
- **WHEN** views exceed rate limits
- **THEN** views are still tracked but rate-limited to prevent abuse

## 4. Technical Context

| Aspect | Value |
|--------|-------|
| Affected Files | `backend/src/app/models/personal_profile.py`, `backend/src/app/api/v1/personal_profile.py`, `backend/src/app/services/personal_profile_service.py`, `frontend/src/services/personalProfileService.ts`, `frontend/src/components/features/profile/ProfileAnalytics.tsx` |
| Dependencies | Redis (rate limiting), PostgreSQL (storage), existing personal profile system |
| Constraints | Must not collect PII, must be performant, must handle high traffic |
| Patterns to Follow | Existing analytics patterns in `profileAnalyticsService.ts`, workspace-scoped data access |

## 5. Non-Goals

- **NOT** implementing a full analytics platform (Google Analytics level)
- **NOT** adding custom domain support (requires DNS/SSL infrastructure changes)
- **NOT** building a photographer directory/marketplace
- **NOT** adding client reviews/ratings system
- **NOT** any AI-powered features mentioned in the feature list
- **NOT** payment processing or e-commerce features

## 6. Implementation Tasks

```tasks
## Phase 1: Database Foundation
- [ ] T001: Create profile_views table migration for tracking view events | File: backend/migrations/versions/0181_profile_views.py
- [ ] T002: Add ProfileView SQLAlchemy model | File: backend/src/app/models/profile_view.py

## Phase 2: Backend Analytics Service
- [ ] T003: Create ProfileAnalyticsRepository for data access | File: backend/src/app/repositories/profile_analytics_repository.py
- [ ] T004: Create ProfileAnalyticsService with view tracking logic | File: backend/src/app/services/profile_analytics_service.py
- [ ] T005: Add view tracking endpoint to public profile API | File: backend/src/app/api/v1/personal_profile.py
- [ ] T006: Add analytics retrieval endpoint (protected) | File: backend/src/app/api/v1/personal_profile.py

## Phase 3: Frontend Integration
- [ ] T007: Add trackProfileView function to personalProfileService | File: frontend/src/services/personalProfileService.ts
- [ ] T008: Add getProfileAnalytics function to personalProfileService | File: frontend/src/services/personalProfileService.ts
- [ ] T009: Create ProfileAnalytics component for settings page | File: frontend/src/components/features/profile/ProfileAnalytics.tsx
- [ ] T010: Integrate analytics component into profile settings | File: frontend/src/pages/settings/ProfileSettingsPage.tsx

## Phase 4: View Tracking Implementation
- [ ] T011: Add view tracking call to PublicPersonalProfilePage | File: frontend/src/pages/public/PublicPersonalProfilePage.tsx
- [ ] T012: Add rate limiting for view tracking API | File: backend/src/app/api/v1/personal_profile.py
```

## 7. Success Metrics

- Profile views are tracked accurately without impacting page load time
- Analytics dashboard loads within 500ms
- View tracking API responds in <100ms
- No PII is collected or stored
- Rate limiting prevents abuse (max 100 views/hour per IP per profile)

## 8. Risks & Mitigations

| Risk | Mitigation |
|------|------------|
| High traffic overwhelming database | Use Redis for real-time counting, batch insert to PostgreSQL |
| Privacy concerns with tracking | Only store anonymized data (hashed IP, country-level geo) |
| Bot traffic inflating view counts | Implement basic bot detection, rate limiting |
| View tracking slowing page load | Make tracking call async, non-blocking |

